and: create\nCreated File with Text:\n```\n# Announcing the Engineering Performance Leaderboard\n\nWe\u2019re introducing a monthly Engineering Performance Leaderboard to celebrate top talent, inspire continuous improvement, and increase transparency and accountability across our org.\n\nThis initiative is data-driven and designed to highlight the impact of our highest contributors while encouraging every engineer and team to level up.\n\n## How it works\n- Metrics: We\u2019ll use a balanced view of activity and impact, including Git contribution signals, code review participation, and sprint delivery/velocity.\n- Cadence: Results will be published monthly.\n- Scope: We\u2019ll highlight both individual contributors and teams to reinforce collaboration as well as excellence.\n\n## Recognition\n- Individuals: Top contributors will be recognized each month.\n- Teams: Team-wide metrics will be included to celebrate collaboration and shared outcomes.\n- Visibility: Results and methodology will be visible to the org to promote clarity and trust.\n\n## Guardrails and fairness\nTo keep the focus on meaningful impact and healthy practices, we will:\n- Emphasize quality and peer feedback alongside activity volume.\n- Review anomalies to reduce gaming and ensure fairness.\n- Iterate transparently on the scoring model based on feedback and outcomes.\n\n## What\u2019s next\n- The first leaderboard will be published next month.\n- We\u2019ll share a dashboard link with methodology and FAQs for full transparency.\n- Managers will use these insights in regular recognition and coaching conversations.\n\n## Call to action\n- Celebrate our top performers when results are published.\n- Review your team\u2019s metrics to identify growth opportunities.\n- Keep sharing knowledge through code reviews and design docs\u2014these contributions matter.\n\nLet\u2019s raise the bar together and recognize the people and teams moving us forward. If you have questions or suggestions on the scoring model, please reach out to Engineering Ops.\n\n```\n, FileEditObservation(content='File created successfully at: /workspace/leaderboard_announcement.md', path='/workspace/leaderboard_announcement.md', prev_exist=False, old_content=None, new_content=None, observation='edit', impl_source='oh_aci', diff='--- /workspace/leaderboard_announcement.md\\n+++ /workspace/leaderboard_announcement.md\\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\\n+# Announcing the Engineering Performance Leaderboard\\n@@ -1,0 +3,32 @@\\n+We\u2019re introducing a monthly Engineering Performance Leaderboard to celebrate top talent, inspire continuous improvement, and increase transparency and accountability across our org.\\n+\\n+This initiative is data-driven and designed to highlight the impact of our highest contributors while encouraging every engineer and team to level up.\\n+\\n+## How it works\\n+- Metrics: We\u2019ll use a balanced view of activity and impact, including Git contribution signals, code review participation, and sprint delivery/velocity.\\n+- Cadence: Results will be published monthly.\\n+- Scope: We\u2019ll highlight both individual contributors and teams to reinforce collaboration as well as excellence.\\n+\\n+## Recognition\\n+- Individuals: Top contributors will be recognized each month.\\n+- Teams: Team-wide metrics will be included to celebrate collaboration and shared outcomes.\\n+- Visibility: Results and methodology will be visible to the org to promote clarity and trust.\\n+\\n+## Guardrails and fairness\\n+To keep the focus on meaningful impact and healthy practices, we will:\\n+- Emphasize quality and peer feedback alongside activity volume.\\n+- Review anomalies to reduce gaming and ensure fairness.\\n+- Iterate transparently on the scoring model based on feedback and outcomes.\\n+\\n+## What\u2019s next\\n+- The first leaderboard will be published next month.\\n+- We\u2019ll share a dashboard link with methodology and FAQs for full transparency.\\n+- Managers will use these insights in regular recognition and coaching conversations.\\n+\\n+## Call to action\\n+- Celebrate our top performers when results are published.\\n+- Review your team\u2019s metrics to identify growth opportunities.\\n+- Keep sharing knowledge through code reviews and design docs\u2014these contributions matter.\\n+\\n+Let\u2019s raise the bar together and recognize the people and teams moving us forward. If you have questions or suggestions on the scoring model, please reach out to Engineering Ops.\\n+', _diff_cache=None), BrowseInteractiveAction(browser_actions=\"goto('http://the-agent-company.com:8092/index.php/apps/files?dir=//Documents')\\nnoop()\", thought='', browsergym_send_msg_to_user='', action='browse_interactive', security_risk=None), BrowserOutputObservation(content='This application requires JavaScript for correct operation. Please [ enable JavaScript ](http://enable-javascript.com/) and reload the page. \\n\\n[ ownCloud 10.1.1 is available. Get more information on how to update. ](https://doc.owncloud.com/server/latest/admin_manual/maintenance/upgrading/upgrade.html)\\n\\n[ There were problems with the code integrity check. More information\u2026 ](/index.php/settings/admin#security-warning)\\n\\n# [ ownCloud  ](/index.php) <::before> Menu  Files \\n\\n<::after>\\n\\ntheagentcompany \\n\\n  * [ Settings ](/index.php/settings/personal)\\n  * [ Users ](/index.php/settings/users)\\n  * [ Help ](/index.php/settings/help)\\n  * [ Log out ](http://the-agent-company.com:8092/index.php/logout?requesttoken=JglwJTcaUhsOWXgVbml9PyscAE5GADoFEUkqKR4HJGU%3D%3AJBGBPBdtBjKVV93LQJdam0O0I0PEKOuQSxJR9hHbCr8%3D)\\n\\n\\n\\n##  No notifications \\n\\nSearch \\n\\n  * [ Files  ](/index.php/apps/files/)\\n  * [ Gallery  ](/index.php/apps/gallery/)\\n  * [ Office  ](/index.php/apps/richdocuments/index)\\n  * [ Text  ](/index.php/apps/files_textviewer/)\\n  * [ Music  ](/index.php/apps/music/)\\n  * [ Market  ](/index.php/apps/market/)\\n\\n\\n\\n  * All files \\n  * Favorites \\n  * Shar